{"parentUuid":"93eef021-5d59-4f7e-b38d-7e40a6533898","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"memoray_proxy: replace per-request fs.stat with fs.watch cache","description":"High/efficiency. In server/lib/memoray_proxy.js, readConfigMemorayBlock does fs.stat on every request. Replace with an fs.watch-invalidated in-memory cache (with a TTL safety fallback for platforms where watch is unreliable). Keep resolveMemoraySettings behavior identical; keep __testing.resetConfigCache.","activeForm":"Fixing memoray_proxy fs.stat bottleneck","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Extract shared createServiceProxy module","description":"Med/design. Create server/lib/service_proxy.js with the common Web-stream piping, header strip sets, and error mapping shared by runtime_proxy.js and memoray_proxy.js. Refactor both proxies to use it without changing external behavior or their __testing exports.","activeForm":"Extracting createServiceProxy","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Remove hardcoded Benny API key fallback, fail-fast in prod","description":"Med/security. runtime_proxy.js DEFAULT_BENNY_API_KEY = 'benny-mesh-2026-auth'. Remove the hardcoded fallback; in production (NODE_ENV/env flag) throw on startup if BENNY_API_KEY (and new BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY) absent. Keep a dev-only default behind an explicit dev flag.","activeForm":"Removing hardcoded API key fallback","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Separate scoped agent credential (server-side scope binding)","description":"High/security full fix. Add BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY. Benny AgentScopeMiddleware derives an effective scope from which key authenticated (agent key => forced sandbox, cannot be widened by header; header may only further restrict). Node: new /api/agent-runtime/* proxy path injecting the agent key + sandbox; /api/runtime/* strips client scope header and injects trusted key. Repoint browser agent runtime client to the agent path. Document residual same-origin isolation gap as ADR follow-up.","activeForm":"Implementing scoped agent credential","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Lint/format pipeline: ESLint+Prettier (Node), Ruff+Black (Python)","description":"Style pillar. Add ESLint+Prettier config for server/ and app/ Node code, Ruff+Black for runtime/ Python, a pre-commit hook, and a CI workflow step that runs them. Match existing code style; do not mass-reformat in a way that explodes the diff—start with config + CI gate.","activeForm":"Setting up lint/format pipeline","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Cloud IaC: Dockerfiles + production docker-compose","description":"DevOps pillar. Dockerfiles for the Node shell, Benny FastAPI runtime, and Memo-Ray Express; a production docker-compose.yml wiring networking, secrets injection (BENNY_API_KEY/BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY), and a CUSTOMWARE_PATH volume. K8s manifests as a later follow-up note.","activeForm":"Writing Dockerfiles and compose","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"StorageProvider abstraction for customware I/O","description":"Architecture pillar. Abstract L1/L2 customware filesystem writes behind a StorageProvider interface with a default local-disk provider, leaving an S3/DB provider as a pluggable implementation. Identify current direct fs writes to CUSTOMWARE_PATH and route them through the interface.","activeForm":"Abstracting StorageProvider","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":7},"type":"attachment","uuid":"453c037f-ab02-44b5-9fcd-c8bbb4923034","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:22:55.609Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"f14181cb-e721-4eeb-b987-5560fe28855c","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"453c037f-ab02-44b5-9fcd-c8bbb4923034","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XWpu197CugaV1eC7zkQg24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_read_input_tokens":186058,"output_tokens":2219,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":355,"output_tokens":2219,"cache_read_input_tokens":186058,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcMm9sNH32TRN1KrzHiXd","type":"assistant","uuid":"8edc038f-3df3-4ed1-a070-bea5dba65172","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:23:03.671Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"f14181cb-e721-4eeb-b987-5560fe28855c","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"8edc038f-3df3-4ed1-a070-bea5dba65172","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XWpu197CugaV1eC7zkQg24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SmuHMS9n5EgtnDLDTLaScE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\architecture\\ADR-003-agent-scope-credential-binding.md","content":"# ADR-003 — Credential-bound agent scope (confused-deputy fix)\n\n- **Status:** Accepted (partial — see Residual Gap)\n- **Date:** 2026-06-24\n- **Supersedes the enforcement mechanism of:** [ADR-001](../runtime/architecture/ADR-001-prime-silo-shell-fork.md) determinism boundary\n- **Related code:** `server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`, `server/lib/service_proxy.js`, `server/router/router.js`, `runtime/benny/api/agent_scope.py`, `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/runtime_client/runtime-client.js`\n\n## Context\n\nADR-001 introduced a determinism boundary: the in-browser agent runtime has full\n*read* access to Benny but its *writes* are confined to `/api/agent_sandbox/`.\nThat boundary was enforced entirely by a client-set header,\n`X-Benny-Agent-Scope`, that the browser's agent runtime *voluntarily* attached.\n\nA code review flagged this as a classic **confused-deputy / privilege\nescalation** vulnerability:\n\n- The space-agent shell proxy injects the trusted `X-Benny-API-Key` on every\n  `/api/runtime/*` call, so the request reaches Benny fully trusted.\n- The proxy then **forwarded the client's `X-Benny-Agent-Scope` unchanged**.\n- Therefore any authenticated caller (or agent-generated code) could simply\n  **omit or alter** the scope header and reach Benny with full, unscoped trust —\n  executing arbitrary swarm/graph/config mutations the sandbox was meant to deny.\n\nTwo further facts sharpened the problem:\n\n1. There is no agent-vs-human identity in the auth layer (`request_context.js`\n   has no role/scope field), so the proxy cannot \"derive scope from RBAC.\"\n2. Benny's `GovernanceMiddleware` is currently disabled (`server.py`), so the\n   API key is not even validated — the scope header was the *only* gate.\n\n## Decision\n\n**Bind scope to a server-injected credential, never to a client header.**\n\n### Two proxy facades (`server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`)\n\n| Facade | Path | Injects | Scope |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | ----- |\n| Human  | `/api/runtime/*`       | `BENNY_API_KEY` (trusted)        | client `X-Benny-Agent-Scope` **stripped** → normal RBAC |\n| Agent  | `/api/agent-runtime/*` | `BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY` (sandbox)  | `X-Benny-Agent-Scope: sandbox` **forced**, overwriting any client value |\n\nHeader filtering and stream piping are centralised in\n`server/lib/service_proxy.js` so the \"drop these client headers, set these\nserver headers\" decision lives in exactly one place.\n\n### Server-side enforcement (`runtime/benny/api/agent_scope.py`)\n\n`AgentScopeMiddleware` now computes an **effective scope** = the *most\nrestrictive* of (a) the scope implied by the authenticating key — the sandbox\nagent key pins the request to `sandbox` — and (b) the header scope. A caller can\nonly **narrow** its confinement (`sandbox → read_only`), never widen it. The\nboundary therefore holds even if the header is forged or the proxy is\nmisconfigured.\n\n### Client routing (`runtime-client.js`)\n\nThe browser runtime client routes to the agent facade automatically whenever an\nagent scope is active (`withAgentScope` / `fetchAsAgent` / a bound client) and to\nthe human facade otherwise. The scope header is still sent for audit/back-compat,\nbut the proxy is authoritative.\n\n### Credential hygiene\n\nThe hardcoded `DEFAULT_BENNY_API_KEY = \"benny-mesh-2026-auth\"` fallback is gone.\nKeys resolve from env with dev-only fallbacks; in production\n(`NODE_ENV=production`) `assertRuntimeProxyConfig()` throws at startup if\n`BENNY_API_KEY` or `BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY` is missing. Set both to the same secret\nin the Benny process and the shell process.\n\n## Residual Gap (why status is \"partial\")\n\nBoth facades are **same-origin**. In-page JavaScript — including agent-generated\ncode — can still *choose* to call `/api/runtime/*` (the human path) instead of\n`/api/agent-runtime/*`. The credential binding makes scope unforgeable *given a\npath*, but it does not stop code from selecting the privileged path.\n\nMaking the boundary truly unbypassable requires the agent runtime to execute\n**isolated from human JS** — e.g. a sandboxed Web Worker or cross-origin iframe\nwhose only channel to Benny is a broker that can reach the agent facade alone,\nwith CSP denying direct `/api/runtime` access. That is a larger change to the\nspace-agent trust model and is tracked as the ADR-001 follow-up.\n\nUntil then, this ADR delivers: (1) scope can no longer be forged by tampering\nwith a header, (2) human and agent traffic carry distinct, scoped credentials,\nand (3) no shipped default key in production.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `tests/runtime_proxy_test.mjs` updated: the human facade now *strips* the\n  client scope; a new test asserts the agent facade forces sandbox + the agent\n  key.\n- Existing `runtime/tests/api/test_agent_sandbox.py` behaviour is preserved\n  (those tests never send the agent key, so header-based behaviour is unchanged).\n- Deployments must provision two secrets; see `docker-compose.yml` / DEVOPS.md.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_read_input_tokens":186058,"output_tokens":2219,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":355,"output_tokens":2219,"cache_read_input_tokens":186058,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke