{"parentUuid":"bb5720f9-ca25-4ecc-a1a7-82e5ae47bf2e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"memoray_proxy: replace per-request fs.stat with fs.watch cache","description":"High/efficiency. In server/lib/memoray_proxy.js, readConfigMemorayBlock does fs.stat on every request. Replace with an fs.watch-invalidated in-memory cache (with a TTL safety fallback for platforms where watch is unreliable). Keep resolveMemoraySettings behavior identical; keep __testing.resetConfigCache.","activeForm":"Fixing memoray_proxy fs.stat bottleneck","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Extract shared createServiceProxy module","description":"Med/design. Create server/lib/service_proxy.js with the common Web-stream piping, header strip sets, and error mapping shared by runtime_proxy.js and memoray_proxy.js. Refactor both proxies to use it without changing external behavior or their __testing exports.","activeForm":"Extracting createServiceProxy","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Remove hardcoded Benny API key fallback, fail-fast in prod","description":"Med/security. runtime_proxy.js DEFAULT_BENNY_API_KEY = 'benny-mesh-2026-auth'. Remove the hardcoded fallback; in production (NODE_ENV/env flag) throw on startup if BENNY_API_KEY (and new BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY) absent. Keep a dev-only default behind an explicit dev flag.","activeForm":"Removing hardcoded API key fallback","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Separate scoped agent credential (server-side scope binding)","description":"High/security full fix. Add BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY. Benny AgentScopeMiddleware derives an effective scope from which key authenticated (agent key => forced sandbox, cannot be widened by header; header may only further restrict). Node: new /api/agent-runtime/* proxy path injecting the agent key + sandbox; /api/runtime/* strips client scope header and injects trusted key. Repoint browser agent runtime client to the agent path. Document residual same-origin isolation gap as ADR follow-up.","activeForm":"Implementing scoped agent credential","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Lint/format pipeline: ESLint+Prettier (Node), Ruff+Black (Python)","description":"Style pillar. Add ESLint+Prettier config for server/ and app/ Node code, Ruff+Black for runtime/ Python, a pre-commit hook, and a CI workflow step that runs them. Match existing code style; do not mass-reformat in a way that explodes the diff—start with config + CI gate.","activeForm":"Setting up lint/format pipeline","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Cloud IaC: Dockerfiles + production docker-compose","description":"DevOps pillar. Dockerfiles for the Node shell, Benny FastAPI runtime, and Memo-Ray Express; a production docker-compose.yml wiring networking, secrets injection (BENNY_API_KEY/BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY), and a CUSTOMWARE_PATH volume. K8s manifests as a later follow-up note.","activeForm":"Writing Dockerfiles and compose","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"StorageProvider abstraction for customware I/O","description":"Architecture pillar. Abstract L1/L2 customware filesystem writes behind a StorageProvider interface with a default local-disk provider, leaving an S3/DB provider as a pluggable implementation. Identify current direct fs writes to CUSTOMWARE_PATH and route them through the interface.","activeForm":"Abstracting StorageProvider","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":7},"type":"attachment","uuid":"51599538-e395-48a6-913a-c0e0a495bdbf","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:25:40.779Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"f14181cb-e721-4eeb-b987-5560fe28855c","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
