{"parentUuid":"2f15be3f-6a38-4a8d-a3ef-ec26d48c138b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\server\\lib\\memoray_proxy.js","snippet":"1\t// Phase M1 — Memo-Ray memory-graph proxy.\n2\t//\n3\t// Forwards /api/memoray/<path> requests from the space-agent shell to the\n4\t// Memo-Ray Express server (default http://127.0.0.1:3030). Memo-Ray is the\n5\t// memory graph of the cognitive mesh — the third first-class graph beside\n6\t// the knowledge graph (documents) and code graph (AST). The shell page,\n7\t// the onscreen-agent `memory-recall` skill, and the `node space memory`\n8\t// CLI all consume Memo-Ray through this one chokepoint, so the endpoint\n9\t// is configurable in exactly one place.\n10\t//\n11\t// The integration is declared in manifests/integrations/memoray.integration.json\n12\t// (schema aamp.integration/1); this module is the `shell_proxy` node of that\n13\t// manifest's process map. Drift between this file and the manifest is a\n14\t// conformance finding (`GET /api/integration_audit`).\n15\t//\n16\t// The proxy:\n17\t//   • Strips the /api/memoray prefix: /api/memoray/beta/overview\n18\t//     → <base>/api/beta/overview.\n19\t//   • Whitelists methods: GET on any path, POST only on /files/open\n20\t//     (Memo-Ray validates open targets against its indexed lineage\n21\t//     server-side — paths outside the memory graph get a 403 upstream).\n22\t//     Everything else → 405.\n23\t//   • Returns 404 {error:\"memoray_disabled\"} when MEMORAY_ENABLED is off,\n24\t//     502 {error:\"memoray_unreachable\"} with a boot hint when the upstream\n25\t//     is down — the page renders both as friendly first-class screens.\n26\t//   • Server-to-server fetch carries no Origin header, so Memo-Ray's\n27\t//     localhost-only CORS policy never applies; browser callers stay on\n28\t//     the shell origin.\n29\t//\n30\t// Configuration resolution per key (most specific wins):\n31\t/