**Lint/CI** — [eslint.config.mjs](prime-silo/eslint.config.mjs), Prettier, Ruff+Black ([pyproject.toml](prime-silo/runtime/pyproject.toml)), [.pre-commit-config.yaml](prime-silo/.pre-commit-config.yaml), [lint.yml](prime-silo/.github/workflows/lint.yml).\n\n**Docker** — [Dockerfile](prime-silo/Dockerfile) (shell), [runtime/Dockerfile](prime-silo/runtime/Dockerfile) (Benny), [memo-ray/Dockerfile](memo-ray/Dockerfile), and a validated [docker-compose.yml](prime-silo/docker-compose.yml) + [.env.example](prime-silo/.env.example).\n\n**StorageProvider** — async seam scaffolded at [server/lib/storage/](prime-silo/server/lib/storage/AGENTS.md) (default `local`, `s3`/`db` reserved). Customware is **not yet migrated** onto it — documented as staged because it requires a sync→async conversion of `file_access.js`.\n\n## Verified\nProxy + scope + view + agent-runtime unit tests all pass (`runtime_proxy`, `memoray_proxy`, `runtime_client_*`, `agent_runtime`); prod fail-fast confirmed; `docker compose config` valid; storage provider smoke-tested; ESLint clean on all new code. Updated the AGENTS.md contracts that described the old pass-through behavior.\n\n## Two things to know\n1. **CI Prettier gate will be red until a one-time `npm run format` pass** — the new gate flags pre-existing legacy formatting (router.js, app.js, runtime-client.js, tests). I deliberately didn't mass-reformat, since that would bury the security diff. Run it as its own commit.\n2. **`BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY` must be identical in the shell and Benny processes** (dev fallback `benny-agent-sandbox-2026-dev`); the compose wires this for you.\n\nI didn't run the Benny pytest suite (no Python venv here), but verified the middleware logic in isolation and confirmed the existing scope tests are preserved by construction (none send the agent key). Want me to do the repo-wide format pass as a separate commit, or start migrating `file_access.js` onto the StorageProvider?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"