{"parentUuid":"7f09972d-c356-4ec0-8676-6cf3a6b12ced","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"memoray_proxy: replace per-request fs.stat with fs.watch cache","description":"High/efficiency. In server/lib/memoray_proxy.js, readConfigMemorayBlock does fs.stat on every request. Replace with an fs.watch-invalidated in-memory cache (with a TTL safety fallback for platforms where watch is unreliable). Keep resolveMemoraySettings behavior identical; keep __testing.resetConfigCache.","activeForm":"Fixing memoray_proxy fs.stat bottleneck","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Extract shared createServiceProxy module","description":"Med/design. Create server/lib/service_proxy.js with the common Web-stream piping, header strip sets, and error mapping shared by runtime_proxy.js and memoray_proxy.js. Refactor both proxies to use it without changing external behavior or their __testing exports.","activeForm":"Extracting createServiceProxy","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Remove hardcoded Benny API key fallback, fail-fast in prod","description":"Med/security. runtime_proxy.js DEFAULT_BENNY_API_KEY = 'benny-mesh-2026-auth'. Remove the hardcoded fallback; in production (NODE_ENV/env flag) throw on startup if BENNY_API_KEY (and new BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY) absent. Keep a dev-only default behind an explicit dev flag.","activeForm":"Removing hardcoded API key fallback","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Separate scoped agent credential (server-side scope binding)","description":"High/security full fix. Add BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY. Benny AgentScopeMiddleware derives an effective scope from which key authenticated (agent key => forced sandbox, cannot be widened by header; header may only further restrict). Node: new /api/agent-runtime/* proxy path injecting the agent key + sandbox; /api/runtime/* strips client scope header and injects trusted ke