ware_git_history_test` (Windows `core.autocrlf=true` → LF↔CRLF on git rollback readback, line 427; was masked before by the commit-count error my await-fix resolved).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":6,"newStart":19,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," **Format pass DONE (repo-wide).** Ran `prettier --write .`; `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` both exit 0. Critical gotchas baked into config: `.prettierignore` excludes `*.yaml`/`*.yml` (the app's custom `yaml-lite` parser rejects Prettier's flow-style — it broke `commands/params.yaml`; restored via git) and `site/` (templated HTML). `eslint.config.mjs` lints only owned code (server/commands/tests + `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/**`); the vendored `_core` tree is ignored. Uses `globals` pkg for node/browser globals; `no-empty` allows empty catch. Every rules-bearing config block MUST have `files` or it pulls the whole tree in."," ","-**StorageProvider migration STARTED.** `writeAppFiles`/`writeAppFile` in `customware/file_access.js` now go through `getStorageProvider()` and are async; caller `api/file_write.js` + tests (`file_write_operations`, `user_folder_quota`, `customware_git_history`) updated to await. Reads/transfer/delete in file_access.js + group_files.js + git_history.js still sync — staged (see `server/lib/storage/AGENTS.md`).","+**StorageProvider migration: all mutating commits done.** `writeAppFiles`, `copyAppPaths`, `moveAppPaths`, `deleteAppPaths` (+singular) in `customware/file_access.js` now go through `getStorageProvider()` and are async. Provider contract extended to preserve fs semantics: `copy(…,{errorOnExist})`, `remove(…,{force})` (force:false = error-on-missing), `move` does EXDEV copy+remove fallback in the local provider. Callers updated to await: `api/file_{write,copy,move,delete}.js`, `api/module_remove.js`; tests `file_write_operations`, `user_folder_quota`, `session_checkpoint`. **Still sync (staged):** reads (`readAppFile`/`buildWriteBuffer`/`listAppPaths` — every reader becomes as