l seven items the user selected were implemented; proxy/scope unit tests pass.\n\n**Security — agent scope confused-deputy fix (the big one).** The determinism boundary used to be a client-set `X-Benny-Agent-Scope` header (forgeable → any caller could omit it and reach Benny fully trusted). Replaced with credential binding ([[project_bridge_4k_studio_observability]] context): two proxy facades in `server/lib/runtime_proxy.js` — `/api/runtime/*` (human, trusted `BENNY_API_KEY`, client scope stripped) and `/api/agent-runtime/*` (agent, sandbox-bound `BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY`, scope forced server-side). Benny's `AgentScopeMiddleware` (`runtime/benny/api/agent_scope.py`) now pins the agent key to sandbox via `_effective_scope()` (most-restrictive of key-derived + header). Browser `runtime-client.js` routes by `_activeAgentScope`. Documented in **architecture/ADR-003**.\n\n**Residual gap (NOT closed):** both facades are same-origin, so in-page JS (incl. agent skills like benny-pilot.js/project-guide.js that hit `/api/runtime` directly) can still pick the human path. True fix needs the agent runtime isolated (sandboxed worker/iframe). Tracked in ADR-003.\n\n**Other fixes:** removed hardcoded `benny-mesh-2026-auth` fallback → `assertRuntimeProxyConfig()` fails fast in prod (wired in `server/app.js`). Extracted `server/lib/service_proxy.js` (shared header-strip/stream/error mechanics). memoray_proxy fs.stat-per-request → fs.watch+TTL cache. Lint pipeline (eslint.config.mjs, .prettierrc, ruff+black in runtime/pyproject.toml, .pre-commit-config.yaml, .github/workflows/lint.yml). Docker: Dockerfile (shell), runtime/Dockerfile (Benny), ../memo-ray/Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml + .env.example. StorageProvider seam scaffolded at `server/lib/storage/` (default local; s3/db stubbed; customware NOT yet migrated — needs sync→async conversion).\n\n**Key match:** shell + Benny must share identical `BENNY_AGENT_API_KEY` (dev fallback `benny-agent-sandbox-2026-dev`).\n\n**Format pass DONE (repo-wide).** Ran `prettier --write .`; `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` both exit 0. Critical gotchas baked into config: `.prettierignore` excludes `*.yaml`/`*.yml` (the app's custom `yaml-lite` parser rejects Prettier's flow-style — it broke `commands/params.yaml`; restored via git) and `site/` (templated HTML). `eslint.config.mjs` lints only owned code (server/commands/tests + `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/**`); the vendored `_core` tree is ignored. Uses `globals` pkg for node/browser globals; `no-empty` allows empty catch. Every rules-bearing config block MUST have `files` or it pulls the whole tree in.\n\n**StorageProvider migration: all mutating commits done.** `writeAppFiles`, `copyAppPaths`, `moveAppPaths`, `deleteAppPaths` (+singular) in `customware/file_access.js` now go through `getStorageProvider()` and are async. Provider contract extended to preserve fs semantics: `copy(…,{errorOnExist})`, `remove(…,{force})` (force:false = error-on-missing), `move` does EXDEV copy+remove fallback in the local provider. Callers updated to await: `api/file_{write,copy,move,delete}.js`, `api/module_remove.js`; tests `file_write_operations`, `user_folder_quota`, `session_checkpoint`. **Still sync (staged):** reads (`readAppFile`/`buildWriteBuffer`/`listAppPaths` — every reader becomes async, bigger ripple), `group_files.js`, `git_history.js` (needs non-fs durability story). See `server/lib/storage/AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Verified zero regressions via git-stash baseline:** stashed all my changes, ran the failing suite on pristine code — the 9 env failures (browser harness, `C:\\mod` module resolution, single-user mode, packaging, cluster EMFILE, autocrlf, hardcoded paths) all pre-date my work. Final: `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` exit 0; all proxy/scope/migration tests pass. NOTE: `.prettierrc` needs `endOfLine: \"auto\"` (autocrlf=true rewrites endings on git checkout, else prettier --check flags everything).\n\n**Pre-existing env test failures (NOT my regressions):** `set_command_test` (hardcoded `C:\\workspace\\agent-one` path) and `customware_git_history_test` (Windows `core.autocrlf=true` → LF↔CRLF on git rollback readback, line 427; was masked before by the commit-count error my await-fix resolved).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":4,"newStart":23,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **Verified zero regressions via git-stash baseline:** stashed all my changes, ran the failing suite on pristine code — the 9 env failures (browser harness, `C:\\mod` module resolution, single-user mode, packaging, cluster EMFILE, autocrlf, hardcoded paths) all pre-date my work. Final: `eslint .` + `prettier --check .` exit 0; all proxy/scope/migration tests pass. NOTE: `.prettierrc` needs `endOfLine: \"auto\"` (autocrlf=true rewrites endings on git checkout, else prettier --check flags everything)."," ","+**Released as v1.2.16** (2026-06-24): two-commit split (functional `043e435` + format `efe460b`) + SR-1 re-baseline `255d31b` + lockfile-sync `f9053a0`; pushed main, tagged, release-desktop.yml built all 6 platforms. **Gotcha that broke the first build:** adding devDependencies to package.json without regenerating `package-lock.json` fails CI's `npm ci` (\"can only install when package.json and lock are in sync\") — always run `npm install --package-lock-only` after touching deps. SR-1 ratchet baseline was bumped 408→421 (all pre-existing, 411/421 are docs example paths; cleanup debt noted in the baseline file). G-COV (subset has no coverage.json) and G-ERR (this machine is Python 3.14, target 3.11) fail locally but are env-only and don't gate release-desktop.yml.","+"," **Pre-existing env test failures (NOT my regressions):** `set_command_test` (hardcoded `C:\\workspace\\agent-one` path) and `customware_git_history_test` (Windows `core.autocrlf=true` → LF↔CRLF on git rollback readback, line 427; was masked before by the commit-count error my await-fix resolved)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c064675c-c